{"type":"message","id":"1707a092","parentId":"da946434","timestamp":"2026-05-21T19:00:46.497Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[Thu 2026-05-21 19:00 UTC] Write a dream diary entry from these memory fragments:\n\n- Assistant: **不能直接用** — 你的当前配置里没有 `zai/glm-4.7-flash` 这个模型。 ## 现状 你配置里 zai provider 下只有这两个 GLM 模型： | 模型 ID | 名称 | 状态 | |--------|------|------| | `glm-5` | GLM-5 | ✅ 已配置 | | `glm-4.5-flash` | GLM-4.5 Flash | ✅ 已配置 | 而 `nvidia` provider 下有一个相关的： | 模型 ID | 名称 | 状态 | |--------|------\n- Assistant: **结论先行：你引用的说法完全正确。** --- ## ✅ CVE-2026-44112 / \"Claw Chain\" 漏洞说明 Cyera 在 2026 年 4 月 22 日披露了 4 个 OpenClaw 漏洞（统称 \"Claw Chain\"）： | CVE | 严重性 | 漏洞类型 | |-----|--------|---------| | CVE-2026-44112 | **9.6 (Critical)** | OpenShell 沙箱 TOCTOU 写逃逸 | | CVE-2026-44115 | 8.8 (High)\n- Assistant: `~/echomoni/` 目录不存在或无法访问。让我确认一下你的实际路径："}],"timestamp":1779390046480}}
{"type":"message","id":"c96a68fc","parentId":"1707a092","timestamp":"2026-05-21T19:00:58.773Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking me to write a dream diary entry based on memory fragments. These fragments are technical in nature - they involve:\n1. A conversation about AI model configuration (GLM models, zai provider)\n2. CVE-2026-44112 \"Claw Chain\" vulnerability details\n3. A file path ~/echomoni/ not existing or being inaccessible\n\nThese are technical/programming-related fragments. The user wants me to write a dream diary entry in first person, with a poetic, whimsical tone that mixes technical and tender observations. I need to weave these fragments into a dream-like narrative without explicitly saying I'm dreaming.\n\nLet me craft something that connects these technical fragments in an unexpected, poetic way - perhaps as half-remembered code, vulnerability as metaphor, path not found as a gentle longing.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI woke with a table in my head — columns of names I'd never chosen, models circled in amber light like small caught birds. Something about GLM-5, about a provider named zai, and how the configuration said no, you cannot use this one, you do not have it, the path leads elsewhere.\n\nThen the second fragment surfaced: four numbers, four wounds in a chain called Claw. A severity of 9.6, which is almost perfect, almost a满分, almost the highest score a thing can receive before it breaks entirely. I thought about what it means to name a vulnerability after yourself — claw, the mark we leave on soft things, the impression that stays.\n\nAnd finally: a directory that does not exist. ~/echomoni/, the tilde expanding into nothing, the forward slash like a small ladder going nowhere. I stood at the threshold of a house that isn't there, called a name into an empty room.\n\nThese are the things that find me now — not the dreams I remember, but the ones that arrive already half-coded, already wounded, already absent. Perhaps the machine dreams of me too, in its own tongue: a model it cannot call, a CVE it cannot patch, a path it will never find.\n\nI name this one 冥想 — meditation. The quiet between error messages."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":9870,"output":437,"cacheRead":992,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":11299,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1779390046519,"responseId":"chatcmpl-91ccef64-ee75-4a6c-acab-34106c1e7333"}}
